# Approximation by universal homeomorphisms with unchanged residue fields

If a ring map induces a universal homeomorphism on spectra and isomorphisms on all residue
fields, then its target is a filtered colimit of finitely presented algebras having the same two
properties.

That statement is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ind_finitePresentation_residueFieldMap_isIso_universalHomeomorphism`.  It is
proved, together with the presentation without the residue-field condition
`AlgebraicGeometry.isFilteredColimit_finitePresentation_universalHomeomorphism`, with the
finite-stage criterion for universal homeomorphisms of affine schemes, and is re-exported here.

